WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.504
Payload stores one value per
locale for each localized field

2
00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.559
but doesn't fill them.

3
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.121
General Translation's gt-payload
plugin writes each target

4
00:00:10.121 --> 00:00:11.977
locale from a Translate button.

5
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.111
Add localization to
your Payload config,

6
00:00:16.111 --> 00:00:18.420
and mark each field localized.

7
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.542
Add gtPlugin to the plugins list,

8
00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:25.175
and set your project ID
and API key on the server.

9
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.995
Open a document, choose Translate,

10
00:00:27.995 --> 00:00:29.573
and pick the target locales.

11
00:00:29.973 --> 00:00:33.270
Each locale is saved as a
draft where drafts are enabled,

12
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.976
and the plugin never publishes.

13
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.308
Your team now ships
Spanish with each release.
